# The thermostat firmware on an STM32F4 Discovery, its USART2 on a TCP port.
#
#   renode --disable-xwt --console -e '$elf=@path/to/thermostat-firmware; $port=8080; include @scripts/embedded/thermostat.resc'
#
# Every byte written to the socket goes to USART2's receiver and every byte
# the firmware transmits comes back. A TMP108 sits on I2C1; the heater and
# relays are PD12-PD15 and PD11 (read them from GPIOD's ODR, 0x40020C14). The line is framed: put
# scripts/embedded/uart-gateway.py in front of it and point clients there.

:name: thermostat
:description: h5i-app thermostat over USART2

$port?=8080

using sysbus
mach create "thermostat"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery.repl
# The temperature sensor the firmware reads: `i2c1.tmp108 Temperature 36.5`.
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "tmp108: Sensors.TMP108 @ i2c1 0x48"
# `false`: no telnet negotiation bytes, the socket carries raw HTTP.
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $port "term" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart2 term
sysbus LoadELF $elf
start
